  "why": "Gnome Village II, by ear. Key pins (audio time, lane 0-3 = D F J K): 0:00-0:18, the contrabassoon's 47 46 43 pattern plays K J F with the 43 on F next to the 46, three keys in a row (user, Nov 27: 'I'm hearing what should be J FD FJ FD or K JF JK JF'). 0:17.6-0:35, the intro's second time, on the cello an octave up: 71 70 67 the same K J F. The dizi's melody, every time it plays (0:35, 1:28.5, 2:20, 2:37.5; user, Nov 27: 'same notes apply wherever this melody plays'): the 78s on one key, J, from the phrase-end hits through the hold and back (J78 F74 D71 J78; '0:37: the Kh and J are the exact same pitches'); 76 74 76 81 F D F K; the run down 78 76 74 73 71 69 67 as K J F D K J F, ending downward ('0:43: ... ends on a DF that should be played down, not up'); 69 71 74 (74) 73 69 71 as D F J J F D F, a three-note walk up to the held 74 and the grace 69 walking up to 71 ('0:43: ... This should just be a three note walk up', '0:45: the FF ... should walk up'); the walk down 80 78 76 74 73 71 68 from the held 71 as K J F D K J F, the score's high 80 trusted ('0:47: let's trust the score here'), then the walk up 71 73 74 76 as D F J K ('0:49: this FJFJ is a walk straight up'); 74 73 74 76 right after the walk up as J F J K, the same keys the walk up gave those notes ('0:50: ... the first and third notes are the same'; 'the walk up is DFJK but followed by exactly matching notes to the top three: JFJK'), and the next 74 73 74 the same J F J ('0:51'). The melody's octave-up statements (0:53, 1:46) take the same keys as the first: 88 86 88 93 F D F K; the run down 90 88 86 85 83 81 79 K J F D K J F; 81 83 86 86 81 83 D F J J D F; the walk down 92 ... 80 K J F D K J F and walk up 83 85 86 88 D F J K; 86 85 86 88 J F J K ('The second time the melody is played didn't get any of the same fixed notes'). 0:33.5, the contrabassoon's first phrase-end hit on J with the cello's four ('0:35: I'm actually missing the first J here'). 0:54.2 and 1:46.8, the 90 that opens the octave-up melody after the held K90 stays on K with it ('can't that top note just be moved to K with nothing else affected?'). 1:10-1:27, the intro pattern's return on the contrabassoon, the same K J F ('1:10~: I should play the bassoon part here'). 2:02.6-2:20, the intro's return: the same keys as the second intro (0:17.7-0:35). 2:49.4, the dizi's last held 71 on F; 2:50.5 to the end, the fadeout's chords: the lower key of each on F, the last on D.",
